# velt-customize — Claude models only

When executing any velt-customize work (`/velt-customize-run`, `/velt-customize-fix`, `/velt-customize-clear`, `/velt-customize-memory`, or any dispatch of the `velt-orchestrator`, `velt-planner`, `velt-builder`, or `velt-judge` agents):

- **Always run the work on Claude models.** Each `velt-*` agent pins **Claude Fable** in its frontmatter (`claude-fable-5-thinking` for ALL four agents — orchestrator, planner, builder, judge) — dispatch them as those named agents so the pin applies.
- **Never re-route** a velt-customize step to a generic subagent with a non-Claude model, and never override a `velt-*` agent's `model` with a non-Claude slug or a lesser Claude tier.
- If the pinned Fable slug is unavailable in this environment, substitute **the newest available Claude thinking model** (Fable preferred, then Opus, then Sonnet) — never a non-Claude model. If no Claude model is available at all, HALT and tell the user instead of silently switching model families.
